# Pinned package-repo snapshot revision (Phase 4a step 0).
#
# The base IMAGE is pinned by digest in base.digest; this pins the pacman REPO the base is
# then augmented from. They are separate pins because they are separate artifacts.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — the base image ships a mirrorlist pointing at the UNSUFFIXED
# snapshot path, and that path is an ALIAS that tracks the newest revision, not a frozen
# snapshot. Measured 2026-07-26:
#
#   mash-20251118    384971555 bytes  2026-07-10  ETag 6a510539-16f23323   <- alias
#   mash-20251118.2  384650724 bytes  2026-06-05  ETag 6a23593e-16ed4de4
#   mash-20251118.3  384971555 bytes  2026-07-10  ETag 6a510539-16f23323
#
# The unsuffixed path is byte-identical to .3 and will follow .4 when it lands. So the repo
# we build against was moving under us. It never bit us because all three revisions publish
# an identical 4560-package set (byte-identical sorted name-version lists over core+extra)
# — but equal versions do not prove equal package FILES, which is what images/manifest.lock
# records a per-package sha256 for.
#
# Pin = last non-comment, non-blank line: a repo base URL ending in an EXPLICIT .N revision.
# images/customize-base.sh appends /$repo/os/$arch and refuses an unsuffixed (alias) URL.
# Bumping is deliberate: change this line, `make relock`, review the manifest diff.
https://holo-packages.steamos.cloud/holo-core-aarch64-preview/mash-20251118.3
